.TH TSORT 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
tsort \- topological sort
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tsort
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tsort
reads
.I file
(or standard input, if
.I file
is omitted or is
.BR \- )
and writes a totally ordered list of items, one per line, that is
consistent with a partial ordering described by the input.
.PP
The input consists of pairs of items (non-empty, whitespace-separated
tokens); the two items of a pair may be separated by any run of
<blank> or <newline> characters. A pair of two different items
indicates that the first must precede the second in the output; a
pair of two identical items only records that item's presence, adding
no ordering constraint. It is an error for the input to contain an
odd number of tokens, since the pairs would not all close.
.PP
When more than one ordering is consistent with the input, ties are
broken by the order in which items were first seen in the input.
.PP
If the input's ordering constraints contain a cycle, no valid total
ordering exists.
.B tsort
detects this, writes to standard output whatever prefix of the
ordering it was able to determine before the cycle blocked further
progress, then reports every item still involved in the unresolved
part of the graph on standard error, and exits with a non-zero
status.
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I file
The pathname of the file to read. If omitted, or given as
.BR \- ,
standard input is used. At most one
.I file
operand may be given.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A complete, cycle-free ordering was produced.
.TP
.B 1
The input contained a cycle, an odd number of tokens, too many
operands, an unreadable file, or an out-of-memory condition.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sort (1)
